Each subscriber with no scan running receives the LAST completed scan's full replay including the terminal 'done' and the server closes the stream in <25 ms (state.events only reset at startScan, index.js:150; res.end() at index.js:225). Combined with the EventSource reconnect loop measured for Finding 1 (new connection + replayed 'done' every ~3 s from one scan), each cycle drives useAtlas's 'done' handler (setScanning true→false + full GET /api/atlas refetch) with no scan running, as filed.

